(6426048, 953439, 66641, '<td valign="top">great, love it</td>', 'great, love it', '2011-05-27 12:15:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426052, 953699, 66384, '<td valign="top">While this is an excellent portrait, and even more so considering minimal editing, I do not think it reflect the style of HCB, as seen in <a href="//www.magnumphotos.com/c.aspx?VP=XSpecific_MAG.BookDetail_VPage&amp;pid=2K7O3R16KTO3" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this book of his portraits</a>.</td>', 'While this is an excellent portrait, and even more so considering minimal editing, I do not think it reflect the style of HCB, as seen in this book of his portraits.', '2011-05-27 12:29:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426054, 953590, 66384, '<td valign="top">While this is a good shot, and HCB had many shots of people leaping or jumping, he was capturing the ''real world''. This shot looks very staged to me, and not at all candid.</td>', 'While this is a good shot, and HCB had many shots of people leaping or jumping, he was capturing the ''real world''. This shot looks very staged to me, and not at all candid.', '2011-05-27 12:35:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426064, 953492, 132010, '<td valign="top">Wonderful photo. I''m having a very hard time judging this challenge but I can believe this photo. I want to believe it. If it was setup I don''t think the photographer would have included the second child. If it is setup, including the second child was brilliant. If that child had been illuminated in that patch of light I would have questioned the photo....to perfect. I''m no Bresson expert by any means but this captures his essence imho. From the setting to the light to the decisive moment this photo works overtime for me.<br/>If this photo is a truly candid shot then I''m in awe of this person''s work. If it is setup it''s still a wonderful shot, just not in the spirit of this challenge.</td>', 'Wonderful photo. I''m having a very hard time judging this challenge but I can believe this photo. I want to believe it. If it was setup I don''t think the photographer would have included the second child. If it is setup, including the second child was brilliant. If that child had been illuminated in that patch of light I would have questioned the photo....to perfect. I''m no Bresson expert by any means but this captures his essence imho. From the setting to the light to the decisive moment this photo works overtime for me.If this photo is a truly candid shot then I''m in awe of this person''s work. If it is setup it''s still a wonderful shot, just not in the spirit of this challenge.', '2011-05-27 12:52:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426091, 952809, 118154, '<td valign="top">Works well for me. 8.</td>', 'Works well for me. 8.', '2011-05-27 13:48:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426092, 952794, 118154, '<td valign="top">Great moment.</td>', 'Great moment.', '2011-05-27 13:48:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426095, 953632, 41337, '<td valign="top">Nice catch.</td>', 'Nice catch.', '2011-05-27 13:49:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426097, 953683, 62357, '<td valign="top">In a class of it''s own!</td>', 'In a class of it''s own!', '2011-05-27 13:50:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426098, 953507, 41337, '<td valign="top">Like the vibe. Nice catch.</td>', 'Like the vibe. Nice catch.', '2011-05-27 13:51:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426110, 953691, 10785, '<td valign="top">I gave this one some thought as to why I was voting slightly blow average. I feel the composition is not donw so well. You have the leading line of the guiderail on the left of the photo taking your eye into the lightpost and the garbage can. That seems to be where the focal point is. Then the couple is looking to the right where the action is, and the edge of the photo is right there. Nothing to explain what they are looking at, or even if you couldn''t fit that in at least some open space on the right in front of the couple could have helped the viewer to ponder something. As it stands the composition is cut off. I really would have recomposed and put the couple on the left side of the frame. Other than that, the grey scale is good. A fairly high amount of midtones with some darker shadows. No real bright highlights.</td>', 'I gave this one some thought as to why I was voting slightly blow average. I feel the composition is not donw so well. You have the leading line of the guiderail on the left of the photo taking your eye into the lightpost and the garbage can. That seems to be where the focal point is. Then the couple is looking to the right where the action is, and the edge of the photo is right there. Nothing to explain what they are looking at, or even if you couldn''t fit that in at least some open space on the right in front of the couple could have helped the viewer to ponder something. As it stands the composition is cut off. I really would have recomposed and put the couple on the left side of the frame. Other than that, the grey scale is good. A fairly high amount of midtones with some darker shadows. No real bright highlights.', '2011-05-27 14:28:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426112, 953674, 10785, '<td valign="top">Good action. Watch the camera''s level. It seems your horizon is tilted.</td>', 'Good action. Watch the camera''s level. It seems your horizon is tilted.', '2011-05-27 14:29:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426114, 953342, 10785, '<td valign="top">Sensor dust is really showing up here. A little closer would have been nicer, cutting out the trck marks n the sand. But you got your shot!</td>', 'Sensor dust is really showing up here. A little closer would have been nicer, cutting out the trck marks n the sand. But you got your shot!', '2011-05-27 14:31:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426116, 953558, 10785, '<td valign="top">Good exposure, some more contrast would have helped out quite a bit. The sign in the window only serves to enhance the story being told! And hey, you even got a post in the middle of the frame... Distinctly Bresson!</td>', 'Good exposure, some more contrast would have helped out quite a bit. The sign in the window only serves to enhance the story being told! And hey, you even got a post in the middle of the frame... Distinctly Bresson!', '2011-05-27 14:34:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426117, 953698, 10785, '<td valign="top">I think this image has all the Bresson qualities. Rhythm and movement with the crowd of people, great B&amp;W tones and a couple sets of female legs, (which I think Bresson may have been a bit of a peeping Tom with the leg shots I have seen of his). I am no afficionado so I am looking at this wondering if I am viewing an actual Bresson image.</td>', 'I think this image has all the Bresson qualities. Rhythm and movement with the crowd of people, great B&W tones and a couple sets of female legs, (which I think Bresson may have been a bit of a peeping Tom with the leg shots I have seen of his). I am no afficionado so I am looking at this wondering if I am viewing an actual Bresson image.', '2011-05-27 14:41:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426118, 953632, 10785, '<td valign="top">I like this for it''s decisive moment... the guy dipping into the fountain is quite funny. But I gotta take point for the use of color!</td>', 'I like this for it''s decisive moment... the guy dipping into the fountain is quite funny. But I gotta take point for the use of color!', '2011-05-27 14:43:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426120, 953231, 10785, '<td valign="top">The camera is tilted on the horizon. It doesn''t look intentional to me.</td>', 'The camera is tilted on the horizon. It doesn''t look intentional to me.', '2011-05-27 14:45:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426122, 953492, 16106, '<td valign="top">Best of the group, nice sense of figure in place which is essential for HCB, and the best moment captured, that sense of action at the point of divergence is just perfect. However this scores, I give you the blue.</td>', 'Best of the group, nice sense of figure in place which is essential for HCB, and the best moment captured, that sense of action at the point of divergence is just perfect. However this scores, I give you the blue.', '2011-05-27 14:45:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426123, 953584, 10785, '<td valign="top">Love those pants!! Really a throwback to the 70''s!!!</td>', 'Love those pants!! Really a throwback to the 70''s!!!', '2011-05-27 14:47:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426125, 953076, 16106, '<td valign="top">My pick for red, just a lovely sweet image, with a very HCB sense of convergence in action of diverse figures. The only thing lacking is that sense of living out in public that is one of the hallmark of the master. Never the less well seen and caught at the right moment.</td>', 'My pick for red, just a lovely sweet image, with a very HCB sense of convergence in action of diverse figures. The only thing lacking is that sense of living out in public that is one of the hallmark of the master. Never the less well seen and caught at the right moment.', '2011-05-27 14:49:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426126, 953184, 10785, '<td valign="top">It just seems like they are wondering if anyone is actually there to greet them. They look so apprehensive to walk in the door.</td>', 'It just seems like they are wondering if anyone is actually there to greet them. They look so apprehensive to walk in the door.', '2011-05-27 14:50:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426137, 953633, 10785, '<td valign="top">Interesting light, intereting pose and figure. Bresson-like, possibly because I''m no expert. Bresson was about the decisive moment and from what I have seen most of his stuff took place out on the street. He was an observer of people and used his camera to do that.</td>', 'Interesting light, intereting pose and figure. Bresson-like, possibly because I''m no expert. Bresson was about the decisive moment and from what I have seen most of his stuff took place out on the street. He was an observer of people and used his camera to do that.', '2011-05-27 15:02:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426177, 953623, 120129, '<td valign="top">This is very sweet and a breath of fresh air in this dark crowd, but the hand shows up strange I think, maybe due to over processing?</td>', 'This is very sweet and a breath of fresh air in this dark crowd, but the hand shows up strange I think, maybe due to over processing?', '2011-05-27 15:37:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426240, 953492, 112739, '<td valign="top">Bumping this to a 9, one of just a few that I felt really caught the HCB feel. (mine certainly did not)!</td>', 'Bumping this to a 9, one of just a few that I felt really caught the HCB feel. (mine certainly did not)!', '2011-05-27 17:29:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426247, 953666, 30896, '<td valign="top">I''m not too happy with the contrast, also the position of the pole is less then perfect, but the scene itself gets plus points :)</td>', 'I''m not too happy with the contrast, also the position of the pole is less then perfect, but the scene itself gets plus points :)', '2011-05-27 17:34:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426251, 953436, 108069, '<td valign="top">HA! This is awesome. Great geometrically, great contrast, and so damn funny. Excellent capture. Oh, and clea... yeah, you know.</td>', 'HA! This is awesome. Great geometrically, great contrast, and so damn funny. Excellent capture. Oh, and clea... yeah, you know.', '2011-05-27 17:55:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426265, 953633, 30896, '<td valign="top">very brave :-) the only non b/w but the play of light does convey st of HCB to me</td>', 'very brave :-) the only non b/w but the play of light does convey st of HCB to me', '2011-05-27 18:23:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426332, 953108, 10785, '<td valign="top">I feel that this is not very representative of the style of Bresson. There are no people in the shot and the sepia was not quite his style. This has an old fashioned victorian feel to it which is nice, but not quite in style... (I do like the subliminal message of the sign though!)</td>', 'I feel that this is not very representative of the style of Bresson. There are no people in the shot and the sepia was not quite his style. This has an old fashioned victorian feel to it which is nice, but not quite in style... (I do like the subliminal message of the sign though!)', '2011-05-27 20:35:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426334, 953076, 36843, '<td valign="top">very cute</td>', 'very cute', '2011-05-27 20:37:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426335, 953052, 10785, '<td valign="top">This would have worked much better had the person been a more prominent part of the image. Bresson inserted himself into the scene through his camera in my opinion. This gives me the feeling the photographer is sneaking up on the person in some way.</td>', 'This would have worked much better had the person been a more prominent part of the image. Bresson inserted himself into the scene through his camera in my opinion. This gives me the feeling the photographer is sneaking up on the person in some way.', '2011-05-27 20:38:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426340, 953657, 39057, '<td valign="top">Great placement on dude sitting in chair in middle.</td>', 'Great placement on dude sitting in chair in middle.', '2011-05-27 20:42:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426343, 953635, 39057, '<td valign="top">Good comp.</td>', 'Good comp.', '2011-05-27 20:44:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426344, 953492, 36843, '<td valign="top">WOW, now this is what I''m talking about</td>', 'WOW, now this is what I''m talking about', '2011-05-27 20:44:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426346, 953436, 39057, '<td valign="top">Come on....dpc people will not get this!</td>', 'Come on....dpc people will not get this!', '2011-05-27 20:45:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426367, 953492, 89723, '<td valign="top">My winner! Fantastic work. You should be very proud of this shot. He is late for something important! Probably heading home from school and will see his dad for the first time in over a year, as his dad is returning from serving his country in an overseas post or he has to go to the bathroom. :) Either way the shot invoke emotion and that''s the essence of Henri Cartier-Bresson. Well Done.</td>', 'My winner! Fantastic work. You should be very proud of this shot. He is late for something important! Probably heading home from school and will see his dad for the first time in over a year, as his dad is returning from serving his country in an overseas post or he has to go to the bathroom. :) Either way the shot invoke emotion and that''s the essence of Henri Cartier-Bresson. Well Done.', '2011-05-27 21:26:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426377, 952607, 89723, '<td valign="top">My yellow ribbon winner! Just fantastic. I want to be a part of that conversation. I bet these are a few trolls of DPC laughing at us ribbon chasers. :)</td>', 'My yellow ribbon winner! Just fantastic. I want to be a part of that conversation. I bet these are a few trolls of DPC laughing at us ribbon chasers. :)', '2011-05-27 21:30:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426380, 953636, 89723, '<td valign="top">One of my favorites of the challenge. Love this interaction. I bet that guy really thinks by petting her dog that he might get a date. ;) No chance! Though she does have that look on her face that says, "If that bag is full of money then maybe you just might have a shot." <br/> <br/>Nice work!</td>', 'One of my favorites of the challenge. Love this interaction. I bet that guy really thinks by petting her dog that he might get a date. ;) No chance! Though she does have that look on her face that says, "If that bag is full of money then maybe you just might have a shot."  Nice work!', '2011-05-27 21:33:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426439, 953154, 30982, '<td valign="top">A decent candid, a cute kid, and a nicely detailed door.  Good exposure and good tones; a bit off on focus on the kid, which is OK in this case.  Not particularly heavy on the "decisive moment" style of HCB in my opinion, though.</td>', 'A decent candid, a cute kid, and a nicely detailed door.  Good exposure and good tones; a bit off on focus on the kid, which is OK in this case.  Not particularly heavy on the "decisive moment" style of HCB in my opinion, though.', '2011-05-27 22:56:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426442, 953657, 30982, '<td valign="top">A simple, everyday moment, with lots to explore, although most of it pretty normal and routine.</td>', 'A simple, everyday moment, with lots to explore, although most of it pretty normal and routine.', '2011-05-27 22:59:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426447, 953086, 30982, '<td valign="top">An HCB-esque title.  Solid documentary shot with good composition, particularly in minimal editing.  Not sure how "decisive" it is, though.</td>', 'An HCB-esque title.  Solid documentary shot with good composition, particularly in minimal editing.  Not sure how "decisive" it is, though.', '2011-05-27 23:00:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426449, 953701, 30982, '<td valign="top">Good tight composition in camera; good expression on your subject and enough stuff around her to give an environmental snapshot.  A nice moment in time.</td>', 'Good tight composition in camera; good expression on your subject and enough stuff around her to give an environmental snapshot.  A nice moment in time.', '2011-05-27 23:02:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426451, 953648, 30982, '<td valign="top">A nice trilogy here.  Interesting that you caught the cigarette glow so well, and I feel sorry for the guy with the giant dot on his head (a shadow, I''m guessing.)  Then there''s the almost kiss just beyond.</td>', 'A nice trilogy here.  Interesting that you caught the cigarette glow so well, and I feel sorry for the guy with the giant dot on his head (a shadow, I''m guessing.)  Then there''s the almost kiss just beyond.', '2011-05-27 23:04:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426453, 953085, 30982, '<td valign="top">I think this might be one of those situations where our friend Henri would have hoped for more "action".  A rather common and plain situation for the most part (other than "boys versus girls" as far as seating choice.)  Minimal means you can''t fix flat lighting (I know - I had the same problem) but editing can''t add a story that isn''t there either.</td>', 'I think this might be one of those situations where our friend Henri would have hoped for more "action".  A rather common and plain situation for the most part (other than "boys versus girls" as far as seating choice.)  Minimal means you can''t fix flat lighting (I know - I had the same problem) but editing can''t add a story that isn''t there either.', '2011-05-27 23:07:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426454, 953008, 30982, '<td valign="top">Nice contrast of the kayak and the person against the backdrop - and nice catch of the water off the paddle.  Not exactly what I''d consider an HCB-esque shot, though I''m not an expert at it either.</td>', 'Nice contrast of the kayak and the person against the backdrop - and nice catch of the water off the paddle.  Not exactly what I''d consider an HCB-esque shot, though I''m not an expert at it either.', '2011-05-27 23:08:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426456, 953636, 30982, '<td valign="top">This makes me smile.  Very nice catch - espeically the uptilt of the dog''s head, the distance of the man reaching to pet him, as though he''s a bit unsure of the animal''s friendliness or of invading the space of the woman on the other end of the leash.  Speaking of the woman - she''s not involved in the moment at all.  It belongs to the dog and the man.  Yet having her in the frame is essential to show the disconnect.  Nicely seen, great work with getting it right with the camera - no edit needed here.</td>', 'This makes me smile.  Very nice catch - espeically the uptilt of the dog''s head, the distance of the man reaching to pet him, as though he''s a bit unsure of the animal''s friendliness or of invading the space of the woman on the other end of the leash.  Speaking of the woman - she''s not involved in the moment at all.  It belongs to the dog and the man.  Yet having her in the frame is essential to show the disconnect.  Nicely seen, great work with getting it right with the camera - no edit needed here.', '2011-05-27 23:10:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426457, 952740, 30982, '<td valign="top">This appears to be posed.  Not to say that HCB didn''t pose people - he did do portraiture, I believe - but this appears to be posed to be an HCB-inspired kind of candid capture, or something like that.  I could be entirely wrong.  Women may hold books like that, sit in long dresses under signs tha say Ladies Waiting Room while looking at their watches... :-)  But to me it appears to be posed, and because of that lacks impact.</td>', 'This appears to be posed.  Not to say that HCB didn''t pose people - he did do portraiture, I believe - but this appears to be posed to be an HCB-inspired kind of candid capture, or something like that.  I could be entirely wrong.  Women may hold books like that, sit in long dresses under signs tha say Ladies Waiting Room while looking at their watches... :-)  But to me it appears to be posed, and because of that lacks impact.', '2011-05-27 23:12:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426460, 953076, 30982, '<td valign="top">Heh!  A summer''s day in any language!  A very good snapshot.  And I do not think "snapshot" is a dirty word or a derogatory term.</td>', 'Heh!  A summer''s day in any language!  A very good snapshot.  And I do not think "snapshot" is a dirty word or a derogatory term.', '2011-05-27 23:16:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426461, 953698, 30982, '<td valign="top">Now THIS is a wonderful "in the style of" or homage to Monsieur Cartier-Bresson.  A simple moment in time.  Busy.  But oh so serene when one joins in with the foremost subject, who in her mind, appears to be all alone there in her chair, soaking up the rays, the grass, the air - enjoying the silence, though it probably isn''t silent... So serene.  But there are other stories, too.  Where do the chairs come from?  Are they first come first served?  Do people bring their own?  What''s to the left, the direction several of the others are looking to?  And all done in a very classic feeling rich B&amp;W.</td>', 'Now THIS is a wonderful "in the style of" or homage to Monsieur Cartier-Bresson.  A simple moment in time.  Busy.  But oh so serene when one joins in with the foremost subject, who in her mind, appears to be all alone there in her chair, soaking up the rays, the grass, the air - enjoying the silence, though it probably isn''t silent... So serene.  But there are other stories, too.  Where do the chairs come from?  Are they first come first served?  Do people bring their own?  What''s to the left, the direction several of the others are looking to?  And all done in a very classic feeling rich B&W.', '2011-05-27 23:20:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426465, 953632, 30982, '<td valign="top">This could be just an average everyday shot if one skips by too fast.  But there''s the guy with his butt in the air doing who knows what - and no one has noticed.  The guy with his head in his hand, wishing he were elsewhere.  The woman next to him, wishing she were someone else.  In my often monochromatic opinion, this would work better in B&amp;W.  Not just because it was how HCB worked, but because it would kill the yellow smiley (even though you feature it in your title) and the orange cone across the way - the only two bits of color I''m not fond of here.  The smiley would still be there, but more subtle...</td>', 'This could be just an average everyday shot if one skips by too fast.  But there''s the guy with his butt in the air doing who knows what - and no one has noticed.  The guy with his head in his hand, wishing he were elsewhere.  The woman next to him, wishing she were someone else.  In my often monochromatic opinion, this would work better in B&W.  Not just because it was how HCB worked, but because it would kill the yellow smiley (even though you feature it in your title) and the orange cone across the way - the only two bits of color I''m not fond of here.  The smiley would still be there, but more subtle...', '2011-05-27 23:22:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426466, 952648, 30982, '<td valign="top">A very good moment caught!  Not just the kiss, but the smile on the woman with the glasses, and the back turned of the guy in the hat.  One wonders if he (the civilian in the hat) realizes he can''t get the girl, but he''d been holding out hope until then....</td>', 'A very good moment caught!  Not just the kiss, but the smile on the woman with the glasses, and the back turned of the guy in the hat.  One wonders if he (the civilian in the hat) realizes he can''t get the girl, but he''d been holding out hope until then....', '2011-05-27 23:24:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426468, 953693, 30982, '<td valign="top">I see you staked out a location and waited for the appropriate shot.  Very good idea!  Perhaps a bit off in the execution in that you''d want your bag lady (not just the sign) to be a bit more in focus if possible (though I do realize HCB didn''t fret focus as much as DPC does).  And given the lighting there, maybe shoot a third or half stop under?  Love the reflections, though.  Makes for a richly layered photograph.  A location worth revisiting.</td>', 'I see you staked out a location and waited for the appropriate shot.  Very good idea!  Perhaps a bit off in the execution in that you''d want your bag lady (not just the sign) to be a bit more in focus if possible (though I do realize HCB didn''t fret focus as much as DPC does).  And given the lighting there, maybe shoot a third or half stop under?  Love the reflections, though.  Makes for a richly layered photograph.  A location worth revisiting.', '2011-05-27 23:26:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426470, 953669, 30982, '<td valign="top">First reaction - I think girls are brave to ride in skirts.  :-)  Not sure how this fits in the HCB repetoire but I kinda get a kick out of the fact the arrows point left, she''s signaling right.  I do think the in-camera sharpening was set too high.  The crisp, almost oversharpened aspect of this doesn''t work for me in this challenge.</td>', 'First reaction - I think girls are brave to ride in skirts.  :-)  Not sure how this fits in the HCB repetoire but I kinda get a kick out of the fact the arrows point left, she''s signaling right.  I do think the in-camera sharpening was set too high.  The crisp, almost oversharpened aspect of this doesn''t work for me in this challenge.', '2011-05-27 23:28:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426498, 953439, 68947, '<td valign="top">Beautiful piece!  It''s enthralling!</td>', 'Beautiful piece!  It''s enthralling!', '2011-05-27 23:48:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426500, 953506, 68947, '<td valign="top">Honestly...it''s interesting angles but, really doesn''t hold any real type of story to it as a lot of Bresson''s work did.  It''s more of a nice angle shot.</td>', 'Honestly...it''s interesting angles but, really doesn''t hold any real type of story to it as a lot of Bresson''s work did.  It''s more of a nice angle shot.', '2011-05-27 23:50:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426502, 953278, 68947, '<td valign="top">A little too busy to see the subjects as clearly as one would hope for a Bresson shot but, it does tell a story.</td>', 'A little too busy to see the subjects as clearly as one would hope for a Bresson shot but, it does tell a story.', '2011-05-27 23:51:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426503, 952607, 68947, '<td valign="top">Has a Bresson feel to it. :)</td>', 'Has a Bresson feel to it. :)', '2011-05-27 23:51:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426505, 953691, 68947, '<td valign="top">I''m drawn to the man in the background, which I think you were likely aiming for the viewer to do.</td>', 'I''m drawn to the man in the background, which I think you were likely aiming for the viewer to do.', '2011-05-27 23:53:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426506, 953684, 68947, '<td valign="top">Awwww....that is such a cute shot.  I love that there''s an intensity to the dog, waiting for its master to come back.</td>', 'Awwww....that is such a cute shot.  I love that there''s an intensity to the dog, waiting for its master to come back.', '2011-05-27 23:53:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426507, 953668, 68947, '<td valign="top">It might be just my monitor but, it''s very darkened...too dark to really see the main subject.</td>', 'It might be just my monitor but, it''s very darkened...too dark to really see the main subject.', '2011-05-27 23:57:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426508, 953657, 68947, '<td valign="top">Beautiful that the one man looking in the direction of the camera....was the one person highlighted by light!  Nicely done.</td>', 'Beautiful that the one man looking in the direction of the camera....was the one person highlighted by light!  Nicely done.', '2011-05-28 00:00:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426509, 952663, 68947, '<td valign="top">I really like this one.  It tells a story, which is what Bresson photographs were about.  Nicely done.</td>', 'I really like this one.  It tells a story, which is what Bresson photographs were about.  Nicely done.', '2011-05-28 00:02:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426510, 953584, 68947, '<td valign="top">Interesting candid shot (what Bresson was about).  Not sure about the pole that seems to run through the head and body of the man facing us but, it makes me wonder what it was that they were looking at and talking about.  Now, I want to know! LOL</td>', 'Interesting candid shot (what Bresson was about).  Not sure about the pole that seems to run through the head and body of the man facing us but, it makes me wonder what it was that they were looking at and talking about.  Now, I want to know! LOL', '2011-05-28 00:02:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426511, 953648, 68947, '<td valign="top">Lovely!  It has a double meaning in contrast.  Really nice.</td>', 'Lovely!  It has a double meaning in contrast.  Really nice.', '2011-05-28 00:02:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426512, 952803, 68947, '<td valign="top">LOL!!!!!  Ok, this one had me chuckling!  Love the title and the photograph, matching up so well.  :)</td>', 'LOL!!!!!  Ok, this one had me chuckling!  Love the title and the photograph, matching up so well.  :)', '2011-05-28 00:02:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426513, 953698, 68947, '<td valign="top">Love this one!  Seems more like a Bresson photograph than a DPC photograph which makes it GREAT! :)</td>', 'Love this one!  Seems more like a Bresson photograph than a DPC photograph which makes it GREAT! :)', '2011-05-28 00:02:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426514, 952751, 68947, '<td valign="top">Engaging photo!</td>', 'Engaging photo!', '2011-05-28 00:02:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426515, 953173, 68947, '<td valign="top">I really love the man in the background!  His face is perfectly lit and contrasted.  It''s a moment captured in his life, wondering what he was thinking.  Hmmmmmmm....now I wish I knew. :)</td>', 'I really love the man in the background!  His face is perfectly lit and contrasted.  It''s a moment captured in his life, wondering what he was thinking.  Hmmmmmmm....now I wish I knew. :)', '2011-05-28 00:02:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426516, 953472, 68947, '<td valign="top">Makes me wonder what they are all waiting for :)  Dancing instructions, perhaps? Lovely piece to ponder on.</td>', 'Makes me wonder what they are all waiting for :)  Dancing instructions, perhaps? Lovely piece to ponder on.', '2011-05-28 00:03:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426518, 953636, 68947, '<td valign="top">Just love this idea and shot!  It tells me that the man is interested in the dog while the woman pays no attention to it.  But, also makes me wonder if the man is waiting for her to get off of the phone to make his "move" LOL.  Really nice capture!</td>', 'Just love this idea and shot!  It tells me that the man is interested in the dog while the woman pays no attention to it.  But, also makes me wonder if the man is waiting for her to get off of the phone to make his "move" LOL.  Really nice capture!', '2011-05-28 00:03:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426520, 953440, 68947, '<td valign="top">Very nicely photographed.  A little to "posed" for though IMHO</td>', 'Very nicely photographed.  A little to "posed" for though IMHO', '2011-05-28 00:03:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426521, 953076, 68947, '<td valign="top">BEAUTIFUL!!!  Heart warming and captures so much!  I hope that you frame this one!  Makes me smile!  If you can...maybe, think of putting this up as "Print Available"????</td>', 'BEAUTIFUL!!!  Heart warming and captures so much!  I hope that you frame this one!  Makes me smile!  If you can...maybe, think of putting this up as "Print Available"????', '2011-05-28 00:03:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426522, 953507, 68947, '<td valign="top">The girl jumping has such a quality to it of lightness.  The contrast of the girl in front (light dress) is a lovely contrast in many different ways.</td>', 'The girl jumping has such a quality to it of lightness.  The contrast of the girl in front (light dress) is a lovely contrast in many different ways.', '2011-05-28 00:03:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426523, 953492, 68947, '<td valign="top">Beautiful piece!  Makes me want to know the story behind this child''s sprint home.  Love the contrast with the lighting, perfectly highlighting the subject and the action capture.  Nice one!</td>', 'Beautiful piece!  Makes me want to know the story behind this child''s sprint home.  Love the contrast with the lighting, perfectly highlighting the subject and the action capture.  Nice one!', '2011-05-28 00:04:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426524, 953701, 68947, '<td valign="top">I am really enjoying looking at the entries in this challenge.  It''s such a wonderful departure from the usual DPC "style" and allows us a very different use of our cameras.  This photo captures a woman in thought, natural surroundings, no glory filled, posed and planned out shots.  Just a woman lost in thought in her usual surroundings. :)  Love it!</td>', 'I am really enjoying looking at the entries in this challenge.  It''s such a wonderful departure from the usual DPC "style" and allows us a very different use of our cameras.  This photo captures a woman in thought, natural surroundings, no glory filled, posed and planned out shots.  Just a woman lost in thought in her usual surroundings. :)  Love it!', '2011-05-28 00:04:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426542, 953666, 30982, '<td valign="top">One thing I noted in a lot of HCB''s work was the juxtaposition of things - nice catch with the sign prohibiting the activity taking place!</td>', 'One thing I noted in a lot of HCB''s work was the juxtaposition of things - nice catch with the sign prohibiting the activity taking place!', '2011-05-28 00:42:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426544, 953702, 30982, '<td valign="top">Strange.  A nod to HCB''s strenght in seeing shape and design, perhaps.  And his passion for painting?  Strange yet interesting.</td>', 'Strange.  A nod to HCB''s strenght in seeing shape and design, perhaps.  And his passion for painting?  Strange yet interesting.', '2011-05-28 00:43:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426545, 953699, 30982, '<td valign="top">I do know he did shoot portraits, and this looks very much like the way he''d shoot one (I have not seen any of his portrait work but didn''t go looking for it either.)  Very real, great light, wonderful expression.</td>', 'I do know he did shoot portraits, and this looks very much like the way he''d shoot one (I have not seen any of his portrait work but didn''t go looking for it either.)  Very real, great light, wonderful expression.', '2011-05-28 00:44:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426546, 953633, 30982, '<td valign="top">I''m going to have to say that I don''t quite "get" this one with respect to HCB but I do find it just odd enough to be somewhat intriguing.</td>', 'I''m going to have to say that I don''t quite "get" this one with respect to HCB but I do find it just odd enough to be somewhat intriguing.', '2011-05-28 00:45:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426547, 953694, 30982, '<td valign="top">I do wonder what HCB would make of the wealth of graffiti these days.  I like the energy of the angle and the excellent contrast here - nice work in camera with that.</td>', 'I do wonder what HCB would make of the wealth of graffiti these days.  I like the energy of the angle and the excellent contrast here - nice work in camera with that.', '2011-05-28 00:46:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426579, 953557, 118154, '<td valign="top">One of my top picks this challenge.</td>', 'One of my top picks this challenge.', '2011-05-28 04:24:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426588, 953626, 113156, '<td valign="top">Very thoughtful expression you have captured, the whole images works really well for me, it would be good if we looked at every detail in life with such intensity and curiosity then perhaps everything would be art and everywhere a gallery.</td>', 'Very thoughtful expression you have captured, the whole images works really well for me, it would be good if we looked at every detail in life with such intensity and curiosity then perhaps everything would be art and everywhere a gallery.', '2011-05-28 05:12:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426600, 953701, 67152, '<td valign="top">such contemplation in her face</td>', 'such contemplation in her face', '2011-05-28 06:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426601, 953173, 67152, '<td valign="top">love the two stories created by the bar down the middle of the frame</td>', 'love the two stories created by the bar down the middle of the frame', '2011-05-28 06:49:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426602, 953626, 67152, '<td valign="top">the interaction of the three forms is magical</td>', 'the interaction of the three forms is magical', '2011-05-28 06:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426674, 953231, 76335, '<td valign="top">I''m not seeing any magic here. It''s a police car passing a person about to cross the street.</td>', 'I''m not seeing any magic here. It''s a police car passing a person about to cross the street.', '2011-05-28 11:11:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426675, 953171, 76335, '<td valign="top">Feels much too voyeuristic for HCB. You did capture the geometry I''m used to seeing in some of his images. Myabe a face would have helped.</td>', 'Feels much too voyeuristic for HCB. You did capture the geometry I''m used to seeing in some of his images. Myabe a face would have helped.', '2011-05-28 11:11:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6426677, 953005, 76335, '<td valign="top">Where''s the decisive moment?</td>', 'Where''s the decisive moment?', '2011-05-28 11:13:20.000000', NULL, 1),
