(6433363, 953492, 36843, '<td valign="top">Thought this might be yours John. Congrats on such a really fine capture, bravo</td>', 'Thought this might be yours John. Congrats on such a really fine capture, bravo', '2011-06-03 16:12:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(6433366, 953433, 61084, '<td valign="top">Well done Steve, and congrats once again. I had a feeling you were due to another ribbon soon. BTW, in regards to your comments on the photo... did you try bumping up the contrast setting a notch or two in camera under the monochrome camera profile settings and perhaps taking the brightness down one notch? I play around with those settings a lot myself, and for a minimal challenge entry I think the results would normally be better compared to a desaturation in software. I also use the color filters  in camera to make certain aspects of the scene pop.<br/> <br/>Personally, with this photo I think the contrast is just fine and added to the appeal of the HCB challenge. Your black point is in a good place when looking at the shadows and his shoes, you can see detail in his jeans and the whites oh his shirt have some detail in the creases etc. I think much more contrast would have brought out elements in the brick such as the patch job to his left that would have been a bit of distraction. As is your subject popped from the background and there is certainly still enough detail in the building/wall behind him to make it pleasing. It helps make it more of a "period" shot in my opinion. Congrats.<br/> <br/>Dave<br/> <br/>ETA: I just read Don''s comment below mine so it appears we are in agreement that the contract level apparently worked well for this challenge in particular...so there you go. LOL.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-06-03 15:16:41.</i></td>', 'Well done Steve, and congrats once again. I had a feeling you were due to another ribbon soon. BTW, in regards to your comments on the photo... did you try bumping up the contrast setting a notch or two in camera under the monochrome camera profile settings and perhaps taking the brightness down one notch? I play around with those settings a lot myself, and for a minimal challenge entry I think the results would normally be better compared to a desaturation in software. I also use the color filters  in camera to make certain aspects of the scene pop. Personally, with this photo I think the contrast is just fine and added to the appeal of the HCB challenge. Your black point is in a good place when looking at the shadows and his shoes, you can see detail in his jeans and the whites oh his shirt have some detail in the creases etc. I think much more contrast would have brought out elements in the brick such as the patch job to his left that would have been a bit of distraction. As is your subject popped from the background and there is certainly still enough detail in the building/wall behind him to make it pleasing. It helps make it more of a "period" shot in my opinion. Congrats. Dave ETA: I just read Don''s comment below mine so it appears we are in agreement that the contract level apparently worked well for this challenge in particular...so there you go. LOL.', '2011-06-03 16:14:47.000000', '2011-06-03 16:16:41.000000', 0),
